WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.585
Messier 4 or M4 is a globular cluster in the constellation of Scorpius.

00:06.017 --> 00:14.434
It was discovered by Philippe Loys de Chéseaux in 1745 and catalogued by Charles Messier in 1764.

00:15.101 --> 00:19.440
It was the first globular cluster in which individual stars were resolved.
